{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>A healing heart is the life of the flesh:</b> From the root meaning life. A heart that is neither angered nor jealous of another is like a healing for bodies. The word \"heart\" draws after it its construct complement — that is, the life of the bodies, for their healing, when they have a healing heart. It is the good and joyful heart that heals the body through its joy." "<b>And rot in the bones:</b> One who is jealous to do evil."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Reading לב מושך as \"the word [לב] draws\"; alternatively could read as \"the heart draws,\" but the context is grammatical, referring to the construct chain חיי בשרים לב."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:52.993353523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}